{"name":"Barrister Grey","hex":"#a2a59e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"barrister","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lawyer with the right to speak and argue as an advocate in higher lawcourts."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barrister"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Barrister","blocks":[{"text":"A barrister is a type of lawyer in common law jurisdictions that originated from the Inns of Court in the medieval English legal system. Barristers mostly specialise in courtroom advocacy and litigation. Their tasks include arguing cases in courts and tribunals, drafting legal pleadings, researching the law and giving legal opinions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Advokat%2C_Engelsk_advokatdr%C3%A4kt%2C_Nordisk_familjebok.png/330px-Advokat%2C_Engelsk_advokatdr%C3%A4kt%2C_Nordisk_familjebok.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barrister","wikidata":"Q808967"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Scottish_Court_wigs_%282013%29.JPG/500px-Scottish_Court_wigs_%282013%2